{
 "version": 1,
 "_about": "Sea step 9 dungeons (core/sea/dungeon_rules.gd, game/sea_dungeon.gd, game/sea_dungeons.gd; LOCKED: hand-made from a room kit, own space behind the door). Each dungeon is drawn from `map` (rows of cells `tile` m: '#' wall, ' ' nothing, any other letter = floor; letters in `legend` are things standing there). Kinds: arrive (where you come in), exit (the gate back out), door (open: 'key' = a key unlocks it for good, 'plates' = while every plate in `plates` is pressed by a player or a block; latch true = stays open once opened, 'lever' = while `lever` is pulled), plate, lever, block (pushed one cell away from you with interact), key (a small key for this dungeon), chest (loot table of data/sea/encounters.json). The space lies at sea coordinates space.first_x + slot x space.step_x, space.y, space.z (far off the map, above the water); a player whose sea y is over indoor_y is inside one. entrance = the gate on the island (sea x, z; yaw degrees; it finds the ground below itself). torch_every: a torch on every n-th wall cell beside a floor. env: the light inside. ALL NAMES / NUMBERS MINE. A dungeon may set its own wall_h (a tall hall: the kit's walls are stretched up, more wall over its doors). Sea step 9c: a fight (kind fight: reach_m, spawns [[x, z]], waves [[enemy ids]], notice) may raise a TIDE (tide = water level per wave over its flood cells [[x0, z0], [x1, z1]]; standing deeper than tide_hurt.from_m hurts dps_per_m per metre); doors 'clear' (fight) / 'free' (+ shut_while = shut while that fight goes on) / 'bigkey' (the Great Key, kind bigkey) / 'sealed' (never; says); a thing on a ledge says on: 'H'; `name` is only for reading. Foes climb ledges at foe_climb_speed m/s. torch_seen_m: torches farther than this from the camera are not drawn (0 = always). dress (sea step 9c-3 art pass): shares of the kit's variant floors (floor_worn, floor_mosaic) and walls (wall_crusted, wall_relief) mixed in by a steady roll per cell, clutter = share of wall-side floor cells given rubble / urns / coral (no collision; kept off doors, blocks' and plates' surroundings). Sea step 9d: outdoor = a puzzle court on its island (at = sea x, z of cell (0, 0), y = its floor), no gate; a lever with tide raises the tide (rafts, tide doors); a chest's piece goes to every player there; pieces: a chart's pieces, joined in the bag when all are in.",
